/-
# Shared definition: right ideals of integral group rings generated by the elements `g - 1`

The right ideal of an integral group ring `ℤG` generated by the elements `g - 1` with `g` in a set
`S`, as a bundled right ideal: Mathlib's `Submodule (MonoidAlgebra ℤ G)ᵐᵒᵖ (MonoidAlgebra ℤ G)`,
the right `ℤG`-submodules of `ℤG`. Shared by the WantedExt statements of Kourovka Notebook Problems
5.10 and 5.28, so that they speak about the same ideals.

For a subgroup `H`, `augmentationRightIdeal H` is the right ideal `I_H·ℤG` of `ℤG` generated by the
augmentation ideal `I_H` of `ℤH` (which is spanned additively by the elements `h - 1`). For
`S = Set.univ` it is the augmentation ideal `I_G` of `ℤG` (the kernel of the augmentation
`ℤG → ℤ`), which as a set is `augmentationIdeal G` of the Kourovka 12.22 entry: the `ℤ`-span of the
elements `g - 1` is already a right ideal.
-/

module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Opposite
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Submodule.Basic
public import Mathlib.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Defs
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Span.Defs

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.GroupRingRightIdealShared

/-- The right ideal of the integral group ring `ℤG` generated by the elements `g - 1` with
`g ∈ S`, as a right `ℤG`-submodule of `ℤG`. -/
noncomputable def augmentationRightIdeal {G : Type*} [Group G] (S : Set G) :
    Submodule (MonoidAlgebra ℤ G)ᵐᵒᵖ (MonoidAlgebra ℤ G) :=
  Submodule.span _ ((fun g => MonoidAlgebra.of ℤ G g - 1) '' S)

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.GroupRingRightIdealShared
